romdev-m2c
==========

This package is a JavaScript port of m2c, the MIPS/PowerPC/ARM/SuperH to C
decompiler, made for romdev. It is a derivative work of m2c and is therefore
licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3 (see LICENSE). It is
kept in its own package so that its GPL terms stay separate from romdev's
MIT-licensed code, which only calls it.

Components and attribution
--------------------------

1. m2c (formerly mips_to_c)
   https://github.com/matt-kempster/m2c
   Ported from commit 1d1c4454a445326541305f83f2b0cb680a9ecb2d.
   Copyright the m2c contributors (Matt Kempster, Simon Lindholm, and others).
   Licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0 (LICENSE).
   src/*.js are module-by-module translations of m2c/*.py; m2c_macros.h is
   copied unchanged.

2. pycparser (m2c's vendored, patched copy m2c_pycparser)
   Not contained in this package: romdev-m2c depends on the separate
   romdev-pycparser package (BSD 3-Clause, Eli Bendersky; PLY by David M.
   Beazley), which is the shared JS port also used by romdev-permuter.

3. CodeWarrior demangler (src/demangle_codewarrior.js)
   Based on demangler.cs by arookas, 3-clause BSD License
   (notice reproduced in the source file), as incorporated in m2c.

Corresponding source: this package ships its complete JavaScript source.
The upstream Python source is available at the URL and commit above.

Graphviz (used only for --visualize SVG output)
   Not contained in this package: the @viz-js/viz npm dependency (MIT
   wrapper, https://github.com/mdaines/viz-js) ships Graphviz compiled to
   WebAssembly. Graphviz is licensed under the Eclipse Public License 1.0
   (https://graphviz.org/license/). It runs as a separate program on the dot
   text m2c produces; no Graphviz code is part of romdev-m2c.
